{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774532351,"nonce":"o1wAQOrozVEnOu4jdkq28zxSBys=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM73ASdj","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/14","origin":"github"},"title":"Deploy project11 on BizzyBoat (gabby)","message":"## Summary\n\nDeploy the ros2_agent_workspace on BizzyBoat's robot computer (gabby, Neousys Nuvo 9160GC) starting from a fresh Ubuntu 24.04 Server install.\n\ngabby will run the ROS 2 autonomy stack using a boat-specific manifest from this repo (`unh_echoboats_project11`), pulling packages from gitcloud — a lightweight Forgejo instance on a private cloud server accessible via VPN.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- gabby has a fresh Ubuntu 24.04 Server installation\n- gabby is physically connected to the BizzyBoat network (LAN on Teltonika RUTX11)\n- An operator machine or direct console access is available for initial setup\n\n## High-Level Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Network and Access\n\n1. **Install ROS 2 Jazzy** on gabby\n2. **Connect gabby to VPN** so it can reach gitcloud\n3. **Configure DNS/hosts** so gabby can resolve gitcloud by name\n4. **Set up SSH keys** for the field account to authenticate with gitcloud\n5. **Verify** gabby can clone a repo from gitcloud\n\n### Phase 2: Workspace Bootstrap\n\n6. **Clone ros2_agent_workspace** as `/home/field/project11`\n7. **Bootstrap from boat manifest** — this repo provides the layer config and repos files, scoped to the layers needed on the boat (underlay, core, platforms, site)\n8. **Switch remotes to gitcloud** using `p11_repo_manager.py` from the site package\n9. **Build the workspace** with `make build`\n\n### Phase 3: Platform Package\n\n10. **Create the `bizzyboat_project11` package** — launch files, config, URDF for BizzyBoat's hardware (see #13)\n11. **Verify launch** — `bizzyboat_launch.py` starts base echoboat nodes plus BizzyBoat-specific sensors\n\n### Phase 4: Site Configuration\n\n12. **Install site-specific configuration** — credentials, network host mappings, and other private config from the site layer\n13. **Configure startup** — tmux session script or systemd for unattended launch\n\n### Phase 5: Verification and Documentation\n\n14. **End-to-end test** — launch on gabby, verify operator station connectivity over both WiFi bridge and VPN paths\n15. **Document the process** — agents log each step as they go; distill into a deployment guide\n\n## Approach\n\nThis deployment will be done interactively — agents and human working together, with agents keeping detailed logs of what was done at each step. These logs will later be used to generate a reusable deployment guide.\n\n## Sub-Issues\n\nSub-issues will be created for each phase or task, linked back here. Tasks involving sensitive details (VPN config, credentials, network specifics) will be tracked in the private site repo.\n\n- [ ] Phase 1: Network and access setup\n- [ ] Phase 2: Workspace bootstrap\n- [ ] #13 — Create bizzyboat_project11 package\n- [ ] Phase 4: Site-specific configuration\n- [ ] Phase 5: Verification and deployment guide\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}